WEBVTT

01:31.530 --> 01:34.970
<i>Ugh. The Chief Editor says he's busy.</i>

01:34.970 --> 01:37.450
<i>How am I going to do my report today?</i>

01:37.670 --> 01:40.410
Oh! Hey, you there! Mister!

01:40.720 --> 01:43.480
You were just looking at 
that building, weren't you?

01:43.480 --> 01:45.770
Are you curious about the Phantom Solitaire?

01:45.770 --> 01:49.460
Or maybe the mysterious young fortune teller?

01:49.460 --> 01:50.580
What?

01:51.250 --> 01:54.480
I see. So a tabloid reporter 
is investigating Polka.

01:55.170 --> 01:57.220
We may be able to learn something from her.

01:57.970 --> 02:01.180
Play along, but don't let her dig too deep.

02:02.010 --> 02:04.070
All right. I got permission.

02:04.070 --> 02:06.140
Yes! Thanks so much!

02:06.570 --> 02:08.850
Okay, let's get started!

02:12.710 --> 02:14.530
Huh? It's kind of chilly.

02:14.810 --> 02:16.360
What?

02:16.620 --> 02:18.340
I sense deep, dark death.

02:18.340 --> 02:24.910
Like I'm facing a cage of fierce beasts.
 No, a completed ting-hu.

02:26.880 --> 02:29.080
They're close.

02:30.050 --> 02:30.800
Huh?

02:34.660 --> 02:37.440
<i>I really want to leave for some reason,</i>

02:37.440 --> 02:38.670
<i>but here goes nothing!</i>

02:39.960 --> 02:43.640
Are you looking for Polka-kun? 
Or maybe Xiaoyu-kun?

02:43.640 --> 02:47.180
You can't see them now, though. 
They're on the clock!

02:48.050 --> 02:51.050
Um... Sakimiya-san, is that you?

02:51.050 --> 02:52.520
Huh? Kochou-chan?!

02:52.520 --> 02:55.480
Do you know this man, then?

02:55.480 --> 02:58.970
And I'm getting crazy chills for some reason.

02:58.970 --> 03:01.340
Hmm. That might not be quite normal.

03:04.740 --> 03:05.860
Soara-san!

03:07.550 --> 03:12.370
You must be the attacker who's 
been scurrying around lately.

03:12.590 --> 03:14.340
Well now.

03:14.340 --> 03:16.670
<i>What is he thinking?!</i>

03:19.360 --> 03:21.590
Would you like a hand, Arahabaki?

03:21.590 --> 03:24.680
Sounds like you're in a great mood, Boss,

03:24.960 --> 03:28.740
but I'll clean up my own mess.

03:28.740 --> 03:29.520
Really?

03:29.860 --> 03:34.480
I thought for sure no one spotted me 
taking out the guys around this building,

03:34.730 --> 03:37.360
but I guess this must be their boss.

03:38.460 --> 03:41.030
Taipei has encountered the phone thief.

03:41.360 --> 03:42.490
Round one.

03:42.490 --> 03:45.450
What? Are you certain?

03:45.700 --> 03:49.480
Heilei soldiers wear clothes 
dipped in a special perfume.

03:50.030 --> 03:54.580
The smell would stick to anyone who 
got close enough to choke them,

03:54.580 --> 03:57.310
and not even daily baths would wash it off.

03:57.950 --> 04:01.010
Taipei's nose can track it for ten days.

04:01.010 --> 04:03.430
<i>And why did he attack in this situation?</i>

04:03.810 --> 04:06.890
To eliminate new threats near Miss Sayo.

04:06.890 --> 04:08.410
That's his excuse, at least.

04:09.070 --> 04:11.350
There are animals more rational than Taipei.

04:11.940 --> 04:14.560
He just wants to fight someone strong.

04:21.110 --> 04:22.990
Whoa! What the hell?!

04:23.210 --> 04:24.190
What's that noise?

04:24.190 --> 04:27.280
Miss! Please stay in your room! It's not safe!

04:27.660 --> 04:31.000
<i>Crap! What the hell is Taipei doing?!</i>

04:33.850 --> 04:35.880
<i>I led the clients outside</i>

04:35.880 --> 04:39.590
<i>and I </i>think<i> Takumi will be safe 
as long as he stays in his room...</i>

04:41.500 --> 04:43.590
Want me to take a side?

04:43.590 --> 04:45.750
For now, take the reporter outside.

04:45.750 --> 04:46.800
Sure thing!

04:47.600 --> 04:49.500
<i>This situation doesn't faze her.</i>

04:49.850 --> 04:51.930
<i>Is that girl another Shinoyama bodyguard?</i>

04:52.630 --> 04:56.400
<i>Between her and this fellow, 
the Shinoyamas have good pawns.</i>

05:03.690 --> 05:05.280
Civil-sama?

05:05.280 --> 05:06.080
Lulu.

05:06.080 --> 05:07.320
Y-Yes?

05:09.240 --> 05:12.240
Hey, come on. It's not safe here.

05:12.240 --> 05:14.540
<i>I can't pass up a scoop this good!</i>

05:14.540 --> 05:15.910
<i>I need at least one shot!</i>

05:23.880 --> 05:26.180
<i>The way he used magic just now...</i>

05:28.900 --> 05:30.560
<i>Sabaramond-san?!</i>

05:32.860 --> 05:34.730
Look well.

05:34.730 --> 05:38.490
People with no talent 
for talking with spirits

05:38.490 --> 05:41.690
use this sly trick to force mana from them.

05:42.100 --> 05:46.420
He steals the elementals' 
mana to fill his own vessel.

05:46.420 --> 05:52.160
But his body will contort and burst if 
it can't withstand his ill-gotten gains.

05:53.150 --> 05:54.010
Hmph.

05:54.010 --> 05:56.000
I'd expect as much from the Elemental Eater,

05:56.000 --> 06:01.380
Arius Sabaramond, 
ranked first among court sorcerers.

06:04.730 --> 06:07.190
You make me sound so sordid, Izliz.

06:07.790 --> 06:09.670
I don't eat them.

06:10.070 --> 06:13.960
I merely borrow power circulating 
through the world for a bit.

06:14.890 --> 06:18.170
I envy you, Corpse God.

06:19.380 --> 06:24.930
You have the love of numerous spirits 
and even a misanthropic witch.

06:25.960 --> 06:28.050
You should give some love of your own,

06:28.050 --> 06:31.130
to many people and numerous skies.

06:31.760 --> 06:35.130
Love is the miracle that conquers all.

06:36.120 --> 06:38.410
Mastering love is beyond me,

06:38.650 --> 06:42.710
so all I can do is pine for the world.

06:41.440 --> 06:44.380
<b>Byadian Imperial Court Sorcerer,
 First Rank

Arius Sabaramond</b>

06:41.440 --> 06:44.380
m 0 0 l 210 0 210 120 0 120

06:44.380 --> 06:46.170
Now, shall we go?

06:47.120 --> 06:50.380
I included compensation for any trouble.

06:51.890 --> 06:52.930
I can't accept this.

06:52.930 --> 06:53.260
It's—

06:56.220 --> 06:58.690
Damn. I got careless.

06:58.690 --> 07:03.400
That hit from you should've wrecked 
a few of his organs, Boss.

07:03.640 --> 07:04.970
Still, you could have dodged it.

07:05.950 --> 07:08.570
I <i>am</i> supposed to be your bodyguard.

07:09.060 --> 07:09.820
What?

07:10.740 --> 07:11.770
<i>Did she...</i>

07:12.170 --> 07:14.810
<i>undergo the same treatment 
as the empire's assassins?</i>

07:15.450 --> 07:19.710
I shouldn't have let you see that, 
but you seem awfully calm, considering.

07:19.710 --> 07:26.170
<i>Oh, right! I'm still using a 
spell to keep my face composed!</i>

07:26.650 --> 07:31.400
I peer into the fates of others. 
This is nothing unusual for me.

07:31.400 --> 07:33.390
Hmm... I see.

07:33.910 --> 07:35.890
Mikoto evidently has a good eye.

07:36.170 --> 07:38.860
Well, we won't keep imposing on you.

07:39.690 --> 07:41.310
Not here, at least.

07:41.770 --> 07:43.850
Arahabaki, look after Lulu.

07:43.850 --> 07:44.620
On it.

07:44.620 --> 07:45.560
O-Okay.

07:45.560 --> 07:46.270
Huh?!

07:50.110 --> 07:51.980
Is it over?

07:51.980 --> 07:53.450
Somehow.

07:54.250 --> 07:57.160
<i>I've never felt an attack like that.</i>

07:57.160 --> 07:58.600
<i>What did he do to me?</i>

08:01.650 --> 08:03.960
Who <i>was</i> that client?

08:04.810 --> 08:07.230
He must be a Bastard Child of Sabaramond,

08:07.230 --> 08:11.680
part of the group the 
Fire-Breathing Bug mentioned.

08:11.680 --> 08:13.420
How can you be so sure?

08:13.760 --> 08:17.930
His looks like someone I know,
 but he isn't him.

08:18.400 --> 08:21.990
His soul is a different hue,
 and he's younger.

08:22.610 --> 08:24.900
But the way he used magic

08:25.320 --> 08:27.390
was too similar for him not to be connected.

08:28.000 --> 08:28.860
To who?

08:29.360 --> 08:34.070
To the head of the court sorcerers,
 Arius Sabaramond-san.

08:37.470 --> 08:38.200
Huh?

08:40.540 --> 08:43.040
Man. Why'd you have to butt in?

08:43.040 --> 08:45.140
You should've left it to me.

08:45.140 --> 08:47.040
Sorry for poaching your prey.

08:47.800 --> 08:51.000
I was just getting warmed up, y'know?

08:51.290 --> 08:52.810
I'm so sorry.

08:53.300 --> 08:56.840
I just thought that I might not 
need to hide my power anymore.

08:57.330 --> 08:58.310
Look here.

08:58.310 --> 09:01.430
Yeah? What about your passport?

09:01.660 --> 09:05.470
I entered the country under my full name.

09:06.160 --> 09:08.380
So it's written right there.

09:08.380 --> 09:12.900
My surname—the name someone 
started using for the organization.

09:13.420 --> 09:15.280
Sabaramond.

09:16.140 --> 09:20.610
So the organization's old-timers 
will panic when they find this.

09:21.850 --> 09:22.970
Hi there, everybody!

09:22.970 --> 09:25.370
Ever heard of the 
"Bastard Children of Sabaramond"?

09:26.480 --> 09:32.210
They're the bad guys who infiltrated the 
police and shot at the Phantom Solitaire!

09:33.000 --> 09:35.840
And, if you can believe it,

09:35.840 --> 09:38.840
the Fire-Breathing Bug's been 
burning their buddies!

09:39.660 --> 09:45.480
If you know the truth, leave a comment 
on this channel, Solitaire TV!

09:45.830 --> 09:48.190
Yeah, I'm sure of it.

09:47.210 --> 09:50.690
<b>Idol
Ryouma Kannagi 

On the set of the latest Sharkborg movie, <i>The Shark Six</i></b>

09:47.210 --> 09:50.690
m 0 0 l 210 0 210 110 0 110

09:48.190 --> 09:50.690
This is a video from one of my concerts,

09:51.020 --> 09:53.780
only the face and voice are someone else's.

09:53.780 --> 09:55.150
What a mystery!

09:55.150 --> 09:57.480
It's one of those so-called deepfakes.

09:57.480 --> 10:00.700
They swapped out the face and voice with CGI.

10:01.220 --> 10:05.440
I wonder who he is, though. Solitaire's son?

10:05.440 --> 10:07.290
And what's "Sabaramond"?

10:07.290 --> 10:10.290
<b>Trend</b>

10:07.290 --> 10:10.290
<b>Sabaramond</b>

10:07.290 --> 10:10.290
<b>Posts</b>

10:07.610 --> 10:10.290
Oh, it's already trending.

10:10.290 --> 10:11.770
I get it now.

10:11.770 --> 10:15.200
The geezers at HQ must be throwing a fit.

10:15.200 --> 10:20.010
Right? And I wrote my name at 
immigration, so they'll tie it to me.

10:20.260 --> 10:25.080
Anyway, are you sure about giving 
the fortune teller that jewelry?

10:25.080 --> 10:27.100
Oh, that's fine.

10:27.100 --> 10:30.290
He might consider it a 
bad deal by now, though.

10:31.290 --> 10:32.730
He's really gone!

10:33.720 --> 10:34.980
Huh? What's up?

10:35.370 --> 10:37.860
I can still sense the soul threads,

10:38.540 --> 10:40.750
but he's definitely been kidnapped!

10:46.100 --> 10:48.210
I see you took a beating.

10:48.210 --> 10:50.180
Forgive me, sir.

10:50.180 --> 10:51.670
No, I don't mind.

10:51.670 --> 10:54.050
We know what our enemies look like.

10:54.050 --> 10:56.880
Now it's our turn to hunt them down.

10:57.260 --> 11:00.040
Um... Was that really wise?

11:00.040 --> 11:01.440
Taking that thing?

11:01.440 --> 11:05.220
Well, that jewelry was 
partly compensation for it.

11:05.660 --> 11:09.710
And if they come to take it back, 
that should be fun in its own way.

11:09.710 --> 11:10.540
Right?

11:10.540 --> 11:12.520
m 0 0 l 210 0 210 70 0 70

11:10.540 --> 11:12.520
<b>Too shocked to move</b>

11:10.540 --> 11:12.520
<b>A Frozen Shark</b>

11:12.520 --> 11:15.400
What're you talking to a plushie for?

11:15.400 --> 11:21.060
A visitor from the homeland may 
be listening to us through it.

11:21.060 --> 11:21.860
Huh?

11:22.150 --> 11:27.490
I asked Lulu who her elemental 
took the most interest in.

11:27.820 --> 11:32.020
The great spirit took 
no notice of the humans.

11:32.020 --> 11:36.710
It was calling out to this 
stuffed animal the entire time.

11:36.710 --> 11:43.890
The elemental's guidance is always abstract, 
but it's never once been pointless.

11:44.430 --> 11:48.350
Polka Shinoyama is likely under the 
influence of a visitor from the homeland.

11:48.350 --> 11:52.440
A sorcerer from another world.

11:52.870 --> 11:54.310
<b>That's right.</b>

11:54.710 --> 12:00.620
Yet the elemental focused on this plushie,
 so it might be a catalyst.

12:00.620 --> 12:02.240
A catalyst, sir?

12:02.780 --> 12:06.100
He put so much effort into 
his fortune-teller get-up,

12:06.100 --> 12:09.470
but he always carried this shark.
 Strange, no?

12:09.470 --> 12:15.460
So maybe the visitor was using this 
to give Polka Shinoyama orders.

12:16.020 --> 12:19.750
I won't <i>know</i> until I examine 
the plushie thoroughly,

12:19.750 --> 12:24.260
but it's almost certainly a key link 
between the sorcerer and Polka Shinoyama.

12:24.320 --> 12:27.010
<b><i>It's funny.</i></b>

12:25.280 --> 12:27.010
<b><i>He's so close
 and yet so far.</i></b>

12:27.010 --> 12:30.330
So I need to investigate it

12:30.730 --> 12:32.810
and protect it, as well.

12:33.260 --> 12:34.230
Why protect it?

12:34.480 --> 12:39.320
If this shark really will connect 
us to the other side of the sky,

12:39.320 --> 12:42.990
then the bugs might try 
to burn it first thing.

12:44.920 --> 12:46.910
Why'd they take him?!

12:47.130 --> 12:48.350
I don't know.

12:48.780 --> 12:53.160
They didn't <i>seem</i> to realize 
that was the real Polka.

12:53.540 --> 12:57.420
I can sense his location, 
so I set a watch on him for now.

12:57.860 --> 13:00.080
<i>I need to find some way to rescue him.</i>

13:02.420 --> 13:05.060
May I have a moment, Master Polka?

13:07.290 --> 13:09.660
And me, too! Excuse me!

13:09.660 --> 13:10.680
Kochou-san?

13:10.680 --> 13:12.310
I'm so sorry!

13:12.310 --> 13:15.230
I thought I was bringing a funky guy along!

13:15.230 --> 13:16.810
Funky?

13:17.100 --> 13:20.570
So you brought him here, Kochou-san?

13:21.050 --> 13:24.610
Why did you attack that person earlier?

13:24.610 --> 13:27.000
A minor issue. Please, pay it no mind.

13:27.000 --> 13:30.950
Are you kidding?!
Who even were those people?!

13:30.950 --> 13:35.130
Master Polka, I hope that you 
will divine that for me, as well.

13:35.910 --> 13:38.330
<b>Fortunes Told</b>

13:35.910 --> 13:38.330
<b>Reception desk opens at 10:00 a.m. 

Please fill out the questionnaire you receive
 with your name, date of birth, etc. 

 We use personal information only for 
fortune-telling and destroy records after.</b>

13:35.910 --> 13:38.330
<b>m 0 0 l 260 0 230 200 0 150</b>

13:38.330 --> 13:40.420
<b>Takeru 
Shinoyama-sama</b>

13:38.600 --> 13:40.420
<i>Polka? It's me.</i>

13:40.420 --> 13:42.050
Takeru-san.

13:42.050 --> 13:44.800
<i>Takeru?! Of Shinoyama Security?!</i>

13:44.800 --> 13:46.670
<i>I heard the details.</i>

13:44.800 --> 13:51.140
<b>Takeru Shinoyama-sama</b>

13:47.050 --> 13:51.140
<i>Those people are dangerous. 
They've attacked our employees before.</i>

13:51.900 --> 13:57.440
<i>Taipei initiated combat so suddenly 
because he couldn't risk your safety.</i>

13:57.440 --> 13:59.860
<i>Of course, his fears proved unfounded.</i>

13:59.860 --> 14:04.030
I see. I sincerely appreciate your concern.

14:04.360 --> 14:09.740
<i>Now, I'd like to call on your 
fortune-telling to identify them.</i>

14:11.700 --> 14:13.030
I understand.

14:13.030 --> 14:15.660
Finding missing persons isn't my specialty,

14:16.080 --> 14:18.530
but I'll see if I receive any guidance.

14:18.530 --> 14:20.830
<i>Oh, but one other thing first.</i>

14:20.830 --> 14:23.170
<i>Solitaire uploaded a bizarre video.</i>

14:23.170 --> 14:23.860
Huh?

14:24.500 --> 14:30.340
<i>If you know the truth, leave a comment 
on this channel, Solitaire TV!</i>

14:31.300 --> 14:33.310
What do you think? Well-made, isn't it?

14:34.010 --> 14:36.290
Why did you make it look like this?

14:35.990 --> 14:44.020
<b>Fire
Safety</b>

14:36.290 --> 14:42.010
If you <i>are</i> close to the Whatever of 
Sabaramond, it should give them a shock.

14:42.010 --> 14:44.040
I'll bet. And what else?

14:44.040 --> 14:44.930
Hmm?

14:45.620 --> 14:48.860
Do you mean to say you need another reason?

14:51.560 --> 14:53.630
What's wrong with this guy?!

14:53.630 --> 14:57.790
Oh! I feel like I've finally 
glimpsed your inner humanity.

14:58.550 --> 15:02.670
I haven't yelled like that since preschool.

15:02.670 --> 15:04.160
Y-You don't say.

15:04.160 --> 15:06.630
<i>Whoa! He got over that quick!</i>

15:06.890 --> 15:09.140
Now, even if I make it out of here alive,

15:09.140 --> 15:12.310
I'll have to get plastic 
surgery and run for it.

15:13.130 --> 15:17.800
So you admit that you're a 
Whatchamacallit of Sabaramond?!

15:17.800 --> 15:21.310
One of them? I wouldn't be 
so sure they see it that way.

15:21.310 --> 15:23.360
I'm just an errand boy.

15:24.290 --> 15:25.830
Fire-Breathing Bug.

15:25.830 --> 15:31.030
Why have you guys been burning 
Sabaramond affiliates for 100 years?

15:31.030 --> 15:33.320
They didn't even tell me that much.

15:33.760 --> 15:34.930
<i>Hi there, everybody!</i>

15:34.930 --> 15:37.490
<i>Ever heard of the 
"Bastard Children of Sabaramond"?</i>

15:37.490 --> 15:43.250
It's been smoldering for a century, 
but this activity is still so sudden.

15:43.560 --> 15:46.180
Those little dears must have finally realized

15:46.180 --> 15:51.080
the best revenge is roundabout, 
by pulling someone down from behind.

15:51.470 --> 15:55.030
I think I'll act, too, then. Let's dance off...

15:55.430 --> 16:01.480
To fetch the little assassin and 
our new sister, Misaki-chan.

16:01.940 --> 16:04.820
You've been burning them for a century?

16:04.820 --> 16:08.490
Why, then, you must be over 100 years ol—

16:08.490 --> 16:09.590
No.

16:09.590 --> 16:14.110
We are no longer anywhere.

16:14.790 --> 16:17.260
Therefore, we are

16:17.260 --> 16:18.470
mistakes.

16:18.470 --> 16:19.630
Impurities.

16:19.630 --> 16:21.540
Those who should not be.

16:22.180 --> 16:23.230
Bugs.

16:23.230 --> 16:24.000
Bugs.

16:24.870 --> 16:26.960
Nonexistent scorch marks.

16:27.250 --> 16:31.170
The same as them. The Bastard Children.

16:31.170 --> 16:36.450
Merely bugs seared into this world.

16:38.370 --> 16:41.980
The Fire-Breathing Bug has been 
active for over 100 years.

16:42.410 --> 16:48.770
So we should be investigating why they're 
hostile to this "Sabaramond" group.

16:47.900 --> 16:50.860
is eating away from the top. 
Don't trust anyone. 

There's another garage on 
the west side of that place. 
The signpost is inside. 

The key is behind the mirror of I-383.

16:47.900 --> 16:50.860
m 0 0 l 400 0 400 300 0 350

16:48.770 --> 16:49.670
But...

16:51.520 --> 16:55.040
Sir, I may have found the case.

16:55.040 --> 16:57.070
Oh! Nice going, Kayakusa!

16:57.790 --> 17:02.940
If the Fire-Breathing Bug doesn't 
just use fire because they enjoy it,

17:03.450 --> 17:08.100
then I figured the cause of their 
revenge might involve fire.

17:08.970 --> 17:10.840
And we might have hit the jackpot.

17:10.840 --> 17:14.870
What's this? A fire in 
Shinjuku 100 years ago?

17:15.260 --> 17:21.600
The corpses of 16 men and women found 
in what looked like adjoining cells?

17:21.880 --> 17:25.960
And half of them seemed like little kids, huh?

17:25.960 --> 17:27.270
Makes me sick.

17:27.270 --> 17:29.060
It's strange.

17:29.370 --> 17:35.530
I'd think I would have heard of such 
a devastating fire at least once.

17:35.750 --> 17:36.800
True.

17:37.530 --> 17:40.840
We have this police file, 
but did the media cover it?

17:41.330 --> 17:44.140
Check newspapers and tabloids from back then.

17:44.140 --> 17:45.000
Yes, sir.

17:45.290 --> 17:47.460
Arase and me will follow Higuro's—

17:48.470 --> 17:49.440
What's up?

17:49.440 --> 17:51.440
<b>GRIN</b>

17:51.440 --> 17:52.920
<b>GRR</b>

17:54.340 --> 17:55.880
No, seriously! What?!

17:58.160 --> 17:59.410
Nothing. Excuse me.

17:59.410 --> 18:02.140
My emotions just got in a car crash.

18:03.150 --> 18:04.730
You, Arase?

18:04.730 --> 18:07.190
It looks like we've found a link

18:07.190 --> 18:09.610
between Solitaire and that organization.

18:11.410 --> 18:16.220
My emotions kind of crashed, 
and they'll take a while to reboot.

18:16.850 --> 18:18.610
<i>Who is this person?</i>

18:18.610 --> 18:22.360
<i>I knew that Solitaire was 
looking for Sabaramond, too.</i>

18:22.360 --> 18:25.830
<i>Has he not met those three yet?</i>

18:26.250 --> 18:30.020
<i>And won't publicizing the name 
"Sabaramond" just make it harder</i>

18:30.020 --> 18:34.550
<i>to tell if people using it are legitimate?</i>

18:34.550 --> 18:36.570
<i>What's his plan?</i>

18:37.280 --> 18:38.680
<b>Nothing</b>

18:39.120 --> 18:43.870
Anyway, I'll need to prepare 
for the fortune telling,

18:44.740 --> 18:50.350
so would you be willing to come back 
in the evening, three days from now?

18:51.780 --> 18:56.410
<i>Does he need to investigate 
before he informs me about them?</i>

18:56.850 --> 19:00.820
<i>If he plans to strike a secret 
deal with that foreigner,</i>

19:01.670 --> 19:05.340
<i>is it about his mother, Kanon-sama?</i>

19:06.450 --> 19:09.760
<i>Taipei is having his fortune 
told for a story, I believe.</i>

19:10.280 --> 19:13.040
<i>If the reporter gives her 
approval, I won't object.</i>

19:13.040 --> 19:14.150
Huh?!

19:14.150 --> 19:16.490
<i>You're dumping this on me?!</i>

19:16.490 --> 19:17.960
<i>But this might work out.</i>

19:18.470 --> 19:21.510
<i>Solitaire, the "Sabaramond" organization...</i>

19:21.510 --> 19:25.350
<i>It all ties back to this building, 
or maybe to the Shinoyama family!</i>

19:25.590 --> 19:27.430
<i>I want time to investigate!</i>

19:27.980 --> 19:30.050
I don't mind either.

19:30.050 --> 19:32.810
How about 6:00 p.m., three days from now?

19:32.810 --> 19:35.160
All right. I'll see you then.

19:35.160 --> 19:38.060
<i>If we're agreed, then this 
is where I leave you.</i>

19:38.060 --> 19:39.490
<i>Bye, Polka.</i>

19:39.490 --> 19:41.030
Oh, sure.

19:41.260 --> 19:45.210
<i>Taipei, return and have 
your injuries examined.</i>

19:45.520 --> 19:46.740
Yes, sir.

19:51.040 --> 19:55.180
Bao, monitor Polka's activities 
for the next three days.

19:55.180 --> 19:56.100
<i>Got it.</i>

19:57.700 --> 20:00.660
We'll leave Sayo to her bodyguard, so...

20:00.660 --> 20:01.340
Yomogi.

20:01.730 --> 20:02.470
Sir.

20:02.470 --> 20:04.080
Investigate that trio.

20:04.080 --> 20:07.190
Don't engage; just find 
out what they're doing.

20:07.550 --> 20:08.660
Understood.

20:08.660 --> 20:10.850
Even if we get Polka to talk,

20:10.850 --> 20:15.440
it's vital that we learn 
their motives, as well.

20:16.020 --> 20:17.660
Depending on what we find,

20:17.660 --> 20:20.020
we may be able to make use of them.

20:22.200 --> 20:25.940
First an abrupt summons, now a rude welcome.

20:26.310 --> 20:30.410
If you want my opinion on that silly video,
 I already emailed it to you.

20:30.730 --> 20:33.190
The elders have summoned you.

20:33.190 --> 20:37.420
Civil-sama, you are to leave the 
country and enter hiding immediately.

20:37.770 --> 20:39.530
And if I refuse?

20:40.040 --> 20:45.530
Since Habaki-dono disappeared, 
we answer to the elders.

20:45.880 --> 20:48.030
Oh? You would use force?

20:48.370 --> 20:51.930
We don't believe that we could 
defeat you or Arahabaki-sama,

20:51.930 --> 20:56.190
but wouldn't you like to avoid a 
stray bullet hitting your attendant?

20:56.730 --> 20:59.190
Um, you really shouldn't! It's not safe!

21:03.110 --> 21:06.450
You must be fools to point weapons at Lulu.

21:08.160 --> 21:11.200
I-Is this more of your power, Civil-sama?!

21:11.200 --> 21:13.980
What? You mean you don't know?

21:15.340 --> 21:16.290
What?!

21:16.630 --> 21:20.130
You mean we can't go rescue the 
real Polka-kun right away?!

21:20.130 --> 21:24.340
Yes. They'll turn the tables 
on us if we aren't careful.

21:24.620 --> 21:28.040
Especially that small girl next to him.

21:28.040 --> 21:30.310
She's possessed by an elemental.

21:30.880 --> 21:34.890
That single spirit might be 
capable of leveling this city.

21:38.830 --> 21:41.290
The elders are so cruel.

21:41.290 --> 21:43.070
I know it's our trump card,

21:43.540 --> 21:46.610
but how could they hide the 
elemental from their own men?

21:49.370 --> 21:52.040
No! Don't kill those people!

21:52.350 --> 21:53.160
No!

21:53.660 --> 21:54.790
Great spirit!
